WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:17.486
Nina was playing Frisbee at summer camp.

2
00:00:17.487 --> 00:00:20.313
But she was thinking about Saturday.

3
00:00:20.314 --> 00:00:25.431
In just two days her family would go to see the town fireworks.

4
00:00:25.432 --> 00:00:30.455
"Mr. Dunn, I love the Fourth of July," Nina said.

5
00:00:30.456 --> 00:00:33.310
"Everything is red, white, and blue.

6
00:00:33.311 --> 00:00:36.885
And fireworks are so cool."

7
00:00:36.886 --> 00:00:41.554
"The Fourth of July is fun, isn't it?" Mr. Dunn said.

8
00:00:41.555 --> 00:00:45.045
"My family always has a big barbecue.

9
00:00:45.046 --> 00:00:48.486
My dad and brothers love to grill."

10
00:00:48.487 --> 00:00:53.494
"My dad loves to grill too!" Bobby said.

11
00:00:53.495 --> 00:00:58.270
"I always eat lots of watermelon on the Fourth," Izzie said.

12
00:00:58.271 --> 00:01:02.121
"You know what the kids in my family do on the Fourth?

13
00:01:02.122 --> 00:01:06.045
They make red-white-and-blue ice pops.

14
00:01:06.046 --> 00:01:11.207
Then they eat them while watching fireworks," said Mr. Dunn.

15
00:01:11.208 --> 00:01:14.896
"Red, white, and blue ice pops?

16
00:01:14.897 --> 00:01:18.532
I bet they're pretty," Nina said.

17
00:01:18.533 --> 00:01:26.269
"Yeah. They're pretty—and pretty easy to make," Mr. Dunn said, chuckling.

18
00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:30.375
"Can we make them at camp?" Nina asked.

19
00:01:30.376 --> 00:01:35.092
"Please? It's almost the Fourth of July."

20
00:01:35.093 --> 00:01:40.287
Mr. Dunn smiled. "That's a great idea, Nina.

21
00:01:40.288 --> 00:01:45.439
I'll bring in everything we need tomorrow."

22
00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:51.798
The next day Mr. Dunn brought in paper cups, wooden craft sticks, and three big bottles.

23
00:01:51.799 --> 00:01:54.597
Nina looked at the bottles.

24
00:01:54.598 --> 00:01:58.272
"Ooh, red juice," she said.

25
00:01:58.273 --> 00:02:01.139
"That's sweet strawberry juice.

26
00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:04.933
Made it myself," Mr. Dunn said.

27
00:02:04.934 --> 00:02:09.389
"Blue juice." Nina picked up another bottle.

28
00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:11.863
"Grape-blueberry blend.

29
00:02:11.864 --> 00:02:15.657
That's cool. And white juice.

30
00:02:15.658 --> 00:02:20.270
Wait a minute—white juice?"

31
00:02:20.271 --> 00:02:21.748
"It's actually coconut milk,"

32
00:02:21.749 --> 00:02:24.861
Jason said, pointing to the label.

33
00:02:24.862 --> 00:02:28.272
"Have you had it before? It's good."

34
00:02:28.273 --> 00:02:30.381
Nina shook her head.

35
00:02:30.382 --> 00:02:33.985
"But I guess I'll try it in the ice pops."

36
00:02:33.986 --> 00:02:39.941
"This will be the easiest recipe you ever prepare," said Mr. Dunn.

37
00:02:39.942 --> 00:02:45.945
"First pour some blue juice into the bottom one-third of the cup."

38
00:02:45.946 --> 00:02:51.599
"The juice has to freeze before we can add the next layer, right?" Jason asked.

39
00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:57.150
"Exactly," said Mr. Dunn. "So let's get started."

40
00:02:57.151 --> 00:03:02.023
The kids filled the bottom of their paper cups with grape-blueberry juice.

41
00:03:02.024 --> 00:03:06.893
Then Mr. Dunn took the cups to the freezer.

42
00:03:06.894 --> 00:03:12.092
"We'll take those out in two hours," he said.

43
00:03:12.093 --> 00:03:16.277
The kids went outside for a nature walk.

44
00:03:16.278 --> 00:03:19.792
When they got back, it was time for the next step.

45
00:03:19.793 --> 00:03:22.961
"Now add the coconut milk.

46
00:03:22.962 --> 00:03:27.716
Fill the middle one-third of your cup," said Mr. Dunn.

47
00:03:27.717 --> 00:03:29.585
"And do it quickly.

48
00:03:29.586 --> 00:03:35.207
We don't want our blue to melt!"

49
00:03:35.208 --> 00:03:40.009
Mr. Dunn hurried to get the ice pops back into the freezer.

50
00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:44.950
Then the kids went outside for their Friday kickball tournament.

51
00:03:44.951 --> 00:03:50.370
In two hours they were back inside, ready to finish making their ice pops.

52
00:03:50.371 --> 00:03:56.682
"Last step: strawberry juice and craft sticks," Mr. Dunn said.

53
00:03:56.683 --> 00:04:01.985
"After you pour the strawberry juice, put your sticks in the cup.

54
00:04:01.986 --> 00:04:05.802
The coconut milk is still a little slushy.

55
00:04:05.803 --> 00:04:12.884
So you can gently push your stick through until it stands up straight," Mr. Dunn said.

56
00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:19.567
"Hurry, get these to the freezer!" Nina said.

57
00:04:19.568 --> 00:04:24.319
While they waited, Mr. Dunn read them a book about fireworks.

58
00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:27.269
Then they all painted fireworks.

59
00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:30.576
Finally the kitchen timer went off.

60
00:04:30.577 --> 00:04:35.646
It was time to take out the ice pops!

61
00:04:35.647 --> 00:04:43.459
Mr. Dunn peeled off the paper cups and handed a pop to each camper.

62
00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:47.695
"Yummy," Izzie said, taking a lick of blue.

63
00:04:47.696 --> 00:04:50.188
Nina licked the white part.

64
00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:55.663
"The coconut milk is good! Thanks, Mr. Dunn."

65
00:04:55.664 --> 00:05:06.259
Nina giggled. "Fourth-of-July fireworks, here I come!"
